    "lawCode": "Amd §§1126, 1132 & 1134, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S273\n\nSPONSOR: GALLIVAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to child abuse in an\neducational setting\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill amends chapter 363 of the laws of 2018 to incorporate bus\ndrivers employed by a school within the provisions of law governing the\nreporting of child abuse to law enforcement as well as make additional\ntechnical amendments.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 1126 of the education law to include bus\ndrivers employed by a school within the child abuse reporting require-\nments.\n\nSection two amends section 1132 of the education law to include bus\ndrivers employed by a school within the training requirements set forth\nregarding the reporting of child abuse in an educational setting to law\nenforcement.\n\nSection three amends section 1134 of the education law by adding the\nOffice of Children and Family Services Statewide Central Register of\nChild Abuse and Maltreatment to the section heading.\n\nSection four establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill makes necessary technical amendments to Chapter 363 of the\nlaws of 2018 that will further enhance protections established under\nsuch chapter for children educated in private schools throughout New\nYork State.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2018, amending the education law relating to\nchild abuse in an educational setting, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S.7372-b and A.8485-b, takes effect.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
